+# Paired-face diagnostic
+
+A privately rendered top-and-skirt preview showed visible stippling compared with its creator reference. Investigation found exact reverse-wound duplicate faces with matching position, UV and skinning attributes. An isolated opt-in candidate culls one orientation only for unambiguous exact pairs; unique or ambiguous faces are untouched. The inspected view appeared smoother. The default renderer remains unchanged.
+
+For two private source scenes, precomputed masks matched recomputed masks across 69 pose/yaw frames each. The isolated paired-mask path measured about 30 ms median versus 53 ms recomputing masks in one bounded local test. A foreground-color heuristic still observed up to 42 apparently lost pixels per frame compared with the original path. Coverage, interior surfaces, mixed meshes, other assets, animation fidelity and native game behavior are not yet proven, so this must remain experimental. Supersampling alone cost more and did not remove the observed artifact. The candidate is not a production recommendation.
+
+245 Rust tests passed and 10 were ignored. Creator content and frames are not included.
